{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Stage Control\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The Stage Control view can be used to manually control an XY Stage and optionally a DOF-5 using a mouse.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 XY Stage Control\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The XY Stage Control continuously monitors your mouse position within the XY grid and updates the stage position to match. You can enable/disable XY Stage Control using the left mouse button. The cross-hair is shown in green when tracking is enabled.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b WARNING: As soon as you enable the XY Stage Control, the stage will move to the current mouse position.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 You can adjust the scale of the XY Stage Control using the keyboard:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab (+) Plus key - Zoom in\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab (-) Minus key - Zoom out\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note that whenever you adjust the scale, it will turn off mouse tracking and re-center the cross-hair.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Zooming in allows you to perform finer motion.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs32 Z Axis Control\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 There are several ways to control the Z axis.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab To control it independently, move the mouse to the Z axis grid and use the left mouse button to enable tracking. This works the same way as the XY Stage Control but only the Z axis will track the mouse.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab When you have XY Stage Control enabled or the mouse is within the Z axis grid you can:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab Use the mouse wheel to jog the Z axis up and down.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab Use the PgUp and PgDn keys to perform fine grained adjustments.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab Use the Home and End keys to perform medium grained adjustments.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab Use the Insert and Delete keys to perform coarse grained adjustments.\sa180\sa180\par}
}